{"name":"Pickle Juice","hex":"#bba528","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pickle juice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The brine or vinegar solution in which dill pickles have been preserved."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickle_juice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pickle juice","blocks":[{"text":"Pickle juice is a mixture of water, vinegar, salt, and spices that is used to preserve food by pickling. It is often consumed by athletes to prevent or relieve muscle cramps."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Tur%C5%9Fu_suyu.jpg/330px-Tur%C5%9Fu_suyu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pickle_juice","wikidata":"Q110611147"},{"title":"Brine","blocks":[{"text":"Brine is a high-concentration solution of salt in water. In diverse contexts, brine may refer to the salt solutions ranging from about 3.5% up to about 26%. Brine forms naturally due to evaporation of ground saline water but it is also generated in the mining of sodium chloride. Brine is used for food processing and cooking, for de-icing of roads and other structures, and in a number of technological processes. It is also a by-product of many industrial processes, such as desalination, so it requires wastewater treatment for proper disposal or further utilization."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Water_salinity_diagram.png/330px-Water_salinity_diagram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brine","wikidata":"Q214403"},{"title":"Juice","blocks":[{"text":"Juice is a drink made from the extraction or pressing of the natural liquid contained in fruit and vegetables. It can also refer to liquids that are flavored with concentrate or other biological food sources like meat or seafood, such as clam juice. Juice is commonly consumed as a beverage or used as an ingredient or flavoring in foods or other beverages, such as smoothies. Juice emerged as a popular beverage choice after the development of pasteurization methods enabled its preservation without using fermentation. The largest fruit juice consumers are New Zealand and Colombia. Fruit juice consumption on average increases with a country's income level."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Orange_juice_1.jpg/330px-Orange_juice_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juice","wikidata":"Q8492"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Pickle_Juice_Drinking_Competition.jpg/500px-Pickle_Juice_Drinking_Competition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Pickle_Juice_Drinking_Competition.jpg/1280px-Pickle_Juice_Drinking_Competition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Pickle_Juice_Drinking_Competition.jpg/500px-Pickle_Juice_Drinking_Competition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Contestants prepare for the Pickle Juice Drinking Competition at Picklesburgh 2022.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APickle_Juice_Drinking_Competition.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Brine_concentration_measurement.jpg/500px-Brine_concentration_measurement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Brine_concentration_measurement.jpg/1280px-Brine_concentration_measurement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Brine_concentration_measurement.jpg/500px-Brine_concentration_mea